# API Configuration — PRODUCTION / LIVE SERVER
#
# Vite loads this automatically during `npm run build` (mode=production) and it
# overrides .env, so a production build never depends on remembering to edit a
# file first.
#
# This file is the ONLY place the deployed API URL is set. The Dockerfile
# deliberately does not pass it as an ENV — a process env var takes priority
# over .env files and would silently override whatever is written here.
#
# Exactly one VITE_API_BASE_URL line may be active. The Jenkins 'Verify Bundle'
# stage greps the built bundle for this value and fails the build if it is
# absent — so the Jenkins parameter default must be kept in step with it.
#
# A relative path, not a host. The browser resolves it against the origin that
# served the page, so the same bundle is correct in dev and in production and
# there is no hostname or port to get wrong. It also removes CORS from the
# picture: the API is same-origin by construction.
#
# THIS REQUIRES nginx to proxy /compliancePortal/ to the backend on the SAME
# origin that serves the UI:
#
#   location /compliancePortal/ { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8099; }
#
# Without that rule the request reaches the static file server instead, which
# answers every unmatched path with index.html — the symptom is a 200 or 304
# carrying HTML where JSON was expected, not an error status.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=/compliancePortal/

